# .graphifyignore — controls what graphify indexes
#
# Strategy: ignore EVERYTHING by default (line below: `*`), then whitelist
# only the source tree. Anything outside src/ is config, generated output,
# documentation, or platform pollution — none of it is code to map.

# 1. Ignore everything
*

# 2. Whitelist the source tree (the only thing graphify should index)
!src/
!src/**

# 3. Defence-in-depth — explicit ignores in case the whitelist ever leaks.
#    These cover folders/files that might appear inside src/ later but
#    should never be indexed for code structure.

# Binary asset directory — 46 landmark photos, zero code structure.
# Indexing these inflates the graph with leaf nodes that have no edges.
src/Images/

# Generated graphify output, in case it ever lands inside src/.
# (Top-level graphify-out/ is already excluded by the `*` rule.)
src/graphify-out/

# Build output / dependencies (in case the project adopts composer or npm later)
src/vendor/
src/node_modules/
src/dist/
src/build/
src/.cache/

# Minified assets — no semantic value
src/**/*.min.css
src/**/*.min.js

# NOTE: src/CSS/style.css is kept in the graph deliberately — it is the
# single stylesheet for the whole app and useful for "where is class X
# defined / used" queries.

# Common project pollution (already covered by `*` but explicit for safety)
.env
.env.*
*.log
*.lock
composer.lock
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Temporary preview / scratch files
palette-preview.html

# Editor / IDE config that some tools leave behind
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
